  "content": {
    "id": "p35-q10",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "10",
    "prompt": "GST is a type of value-added tax (VAT). For these questions, assume that each purchase qualifies for a refund of the full tax amount and that each stated purchase price includes tax. The Australian GST shortcuts apply to a 10% tax rate.\nUse the unitary method to answer these questions. Give non-integer monetary answers to 2 decimal places.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p35-q10-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "The GST in Australia is 10%.\nIf a tourist paid \\$1200 for an iPhone, how much GST would they get refunded?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "\\$109.09; the included GST is \\$1200 ÷ 11.",
          "worked": "\\$1200 represents 110% of the pre-GST price.\n$$\\begin{align*}110\\%&=\\$1200\\\\10\\%&=\\frac{\\$1200}{11}\\\\10\\%&\\approx\\$109.09\\end{align*}$$\nThe GST refund is \\$109.09.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 29
      },
      {
        "id": "p35-q10-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "The VAT in Thailand is 7%. Mr Ding bought his mum a scarf for ฿4800.\nHow much VAT would he get refunded?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "฿314.02; find 1% by dividing ฿4800 by 107, then multiply by 7.",
          "worked": "฿4800 represents 107% of the pre-tax price.\n$$\\begin{align*}107\\%&=4800\\text{ baht}\\\\1\\%&=\\frac{4800}{107}\\text{ baht}\\\\7\\%&=\\frac{4800\\times7}{107}\\text{ baht}\\\\7\\%&\\approx314.02\\text{ baht}\\end{align*}$$\nThe VAT refund is ฿314.02.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 36
      },
      {
        "id": "p35-q10-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "The VAT in Japan is 10%. Mr Ding bought some soft toys for ¥24 000.\nHow much VAT would he get refunded?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "¥2181.82; the included VAT is ¥24 000 ÷ 11.",
          "worked": "¥24 000 represents 110% of the pre-tax price.\n$$\\begin{align*}110\\%&=24000\\text{ yen}\\\\10\\%&=\\frac{24000}{11}\\text{ yen}\\\\10\\%&\\approx2181.82\\text{ yen}\\end{align*}$$\nThe VAT refund is ¥2181.82, to 2 decimal places.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 29
      },
      {
        "id": "p35-q10-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "The VAT in New Zealand is 15%. A tourist was refunded \\$90.\nWhat was the VAT-inclusive value of the merchandise they bought?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "\\$690; \\$90 ÷ 15 × 115.",
          "worked": "The \\$90 refund represents 15% of the pre-tax price. The tax-inclusive value represents 115%.\n$$\\begin{align*}15\\%&=\\$90\\\\1\\%&=\\$90\\div15=\\$6\\\\115\\%&=\\$6\\times115=\\$690\\end{align*}$$\nThe VAT-inclusive value is \\$690.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 28
      },
      {
        "id": "p35-q10-e",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "The VAT in the UK is 20%. A tourist got refunded £144 for a laptop they bought.\nWhat was the VAT-inclusive value of the laptop?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "£864; £144 ÷ 20 × 120.",
          "worked": "The £144 refund represents 20% of the pre-tax price. The tax-inclusive value represents 120%.\n$$\\begin{align*}20\\%&=144\\text{ pounds}\\\\1\\%&=144\\div20=7.2\\text{ pounds}\\\\120\\%&=7.2\\times120=864\\text{ pounds}\\end{align*}$$\nThe VAT-inclusive value is £864.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 28
      }
    ]
  },
